<title>INDIA: India state-owned banks come out of red in 96/97.</title>
<headline>India state-owned banks come out of red in 96/97.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-owned banks posted a combined  net profit of 30.09 billion rupees ($840 million) in 1996/97 (April-March)  compared with a loss of 3.71 billion the previous year, the junior  minister of finance said on Friday.</p>
<p>According to the Reserve Bank of India, profits of state-owned banks  grew due to better fund management, reductions in non-performing assets  (NPAs) or bad loans, and improved recovery of NPAs, Minister Satpal  Maharaj told the lower house of parliament.</p>
<p>India has 27 state-owned banks.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
<p>($1 = 35.8 rupees)</p>
